feat(phase4): turn mechanics, battle declaration + resolution dice

Add the turn/phase loop and combat setup:
- Phase state machine: Draw -> Main -> Battle -> Resolution -> End,
  with a turn counter, TurnHud strip + Next Phase button, and a
  PhaseBanner that slides in/holds/out on every phase change.
- Draw auto-draws to 6 (else 1) then advances; End folds replen back
  into the deck and graveyards non-continuous B cards.
- Card placement gated to Main; manual deck-click draw disabled.
- Battle: click either linked A/C zone to declare that column's A card
  as an attacker (gold outline across the whole column). Only occupied
  A columns can attack.
- Resolution: each declared attacker rolls a D20 simultaneously over its
  A/C link area (in-scene, face-snaps toward the camera on settle), values
  absorbed into lastRolls, then auto-advances to End. Dice wait for the
  Resolution banner to clear before tumbling.
- Placement: dragging an A/C card highlights and accepts a drop on either
  zone of a linked column, resolving to the card's correct slot.

